1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,700
Three days in Seoul.

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:03,840
Palaces, markets

3
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:05,400
a city view at sunset

4
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:08,080
and one day that's completely yours.

5
00:00:09,114 --> 00:00:10,907
If this is your first time

6
00:00:10,907 --> 00:00:13,490
this plan keeps each day in one part of

7
00:00:13,490 --> 00:00:14,123
the city

8
00:00:14,123 --> 00:00:16,548
so you spend your time looking around

9
00:00:16,548 --> 00:00:17,813
not changing trains.

10
00:00:17,813 --> 00:00:20,291
I'll show you the route for every day

11
00:00:20,291 --> 00:00:21,134
what to eat

12
00:00:21,134 --> 00:00:24,914
and the small mistakes that trip up first-time visitors.

13
00:00:25,476 --> 00:00:27,656
Let's start with a few things to sort out

14
00:00:27,656 --> 00:00:28,916
before day one.

15
00:00:29,742 --> 00:00:30,722
First

16
00:00:30,722 --> 00:00:32,622
check your dates.

17
00:00:32,622 --> 00:00:35,242
Gyeongbokgung Palace is closed on Tuesdays

18
00:00:35,242 --> 00:00:38,262
and Changdeokgung Palace is closed on Mondays.

19
00:00:38,262 --> 00:00:40,062
If your trip falls that way

20
00:00:40,062 --> 00:00:42,322
just swap day one and day three.

21
00:00:42,696 --> 00:00:43,816
Second

22
00:00:43,816 --> 00:00:46,236
get a transit card when you arrive.

23
00:00:46,236 --> 00:00:48,656
You tap it on the subway and on buses

24
00:00:48,656 --> 00:00:51,936
and transfers within a short time are discounted.

25
00:00:52,266 --> 00:00:52,774
Third

26
00:00:52,774 --> 00:00:55,059
install Naver Map or KakaoMap.

27
00:00:55,059 --> 00:00:58,232
Google Maps can show you places in Korea

28
00:00:58,232 --> 00:01:00,580
but its directions are limited

29
00:01:00,580 --> 00:01:03,437
so a Korean map app will save you a

30
00:01:03,437 --> 00:01:05,006
lot of guessing.

31
00:01:05,676 --> 00:01:08,516
And where should you stay?

32
00:01:08,516 --> 00:01:12,096
Central Seoul works best for this plan.

33
00:01:12,096 --> 00:01:14,296
Around Gwanghwamun, Jongno

34
00:01:14,296 --> 00:01:16,516
City Hall or Myeongdong

35
00:01:16,516 --> 00:01:19,416
every stop is a short subway ride or a

36
00:01:19,416 --> 00:01:20,076
walk away.

37
00:01:20,478 --> 00:01:23,218
Day one is all about old Seoul

38
00:01:23,218 --> 00:01:26,158
and you can do the whole day on foot.

39
00:01:26,592 --> 00:01:29,692
Start early at Gyeongbokgung Palace

40
00:01:29,692 --> 00:01:32,632
the largest of Seoul's royal palaces from the

41
00:01:32,632 --> 00:01:34,672
Joseon dynasty.

42
00:01:34,672 --> 00:01:38,232
Get off at Gyeongbokgung Station on Line 3.

43
00:01:38,232 --> 00:01:40,352
If you arrive around opening time

44
00:01:40,352 --> 00:01:42,672
the big courtyards are much quieter.

45
00:01:43,098 --> 00:01:45,858
The changing of the royal guard at Gwanghwamun

46
00:01:45,858 --> 00:01:48,578
Gate usually happens at ten in the morning and

47
00:01:48,578 --> 00:01:50,098
two in the afternoon.

48
00:01:50,098 --> 00:01:51,578
And here's a fun one:

49
00:01:51,578 --> 00:01:52,898
if you wear hanbok

50
00:01:52,898 --> 00:01:54,298
the traditional dress

51
00:01:54,298 --> 00:01:56,338
entry to the palaces is free.

52
00:01:56,338 --> 00:01:58,198
There are rental shops near the station.

53
00:01:58,596 --> 00:02:01,016
Give the palace about two hours.

54
00:02:01,016 --> 00:02:03,516
Then walk east to Anguk and the hanok lanes

55
00:02:03,516 --> 00:02:04,816
of Bukchon.

56
00:02:04,816 --> 00:02:06,076
These are real homes

57
00:02:06,076 --> 00:02:09,296
so keep your voice down and stay out of doorways.

58
00:02:09,296 --> 00:02:11,376
Some parts of Bukchon now have visiting hours

59
00:02:11,376 --> 00:02:12,516
for tourists

60
00:02:12,516 --> 00:02:14,196
so check the signs as you go.

61
00:02:14,646 --> 00:02:15,899
In the afternoon

62
00:02:15,899 --> 00:02:18,585
head a few minutes south to Insadong.

63
00:02:18,585 --> 00:02:21,809
The main street and its side alleys are full

64
00:02:21,809 --> 00:02:23,361
of traditional crafts

65
00:02:23,361 --> 00:02:25,569
tea houses and small galleries.

66
00:02:25,569 --> 00:02:28,315
It's a good place for small souvenirs

67
00:02:28,315 --> 00:02:30,286
like hanji paper goods.

68
00:02:30,696 --> 00:02:33,896
Finish with an evening walk along Cheonggyecheon

69
00:02:33,896 --> 00:02:36,136
the stream that runs below street level from

70
00:02:36,136 --> 00:02:37,576
Cheonggye Plaza.

71
00:02:37,576 --> 00:02:39,016
It's lit up after dark

72
00:02:39,016 --> 00:02:39,676
it's free

73
00:02:39,676 --> 00:02:41,736
and it's an easy way to end a long

74
00:02:41,736 --> 00:02:42,656
first day.

75
00:02:43,266 --> 00:02:45,926
Day two is for food

76
00:02:45,926 --> 00:02:48,366
shopping and the best view of the city.

77
00:02:48,828 --> 00:02:50,761
Start at Gwangjang Market

78
00:02:50,761 --> 00:02:53,443
near Jongno 5-ga Station on Line 1.

79
00:02:53,443 --> 00:02:56,936
It's one of Seoul's oldest markets and a great

80
00:02:56,936 --> 00:02:59,805
place for breakfast or an early lunch.

81
00:02:59,805 --> 00:03:01,364
Look for bindaetteok

82
00:03:01,364 --> 00:03:05,293
a crispy mung bean pancake fried right at the stall

83
00:03:05,293 --> 00:03:06,603
and mayak gimbap

84
00:03:06,603 --> 00:03:10,158
little rice rolls that are hard to stop eating.

85
00:03:10,158 --> 00:03:12,828
Bring some cash for the stalls.

86
00:03:13,326 --> 00:03:18,026
Then take the subway to Myeongdong on Line 4.

87
00:03:18,026 --> 00:03:21,326
It's packed with cosmetics shops and fashion stores

88
00:03:21,326 --> 00:03:25,146
and from late afternoon the street food stalls open.

89
00:03:25,146 --> 00:03:28,106
Many shops offer tax refunds for visitors

90
00:03:28,106 --> 00:03:30,566
so bring your passport when you go shopping.

91
00:03:31,128 --> 00:03:32,805
As the sun goes down

92
00:03:32,805 --> 00:03:35,165
go up Namsan to N Seoul Tower.

93
00:03:35,165 --> 00:03:38,642
From Myeongdong you can walk to the cable car

94
00:03:38,642 --> 00:03:41,002
or take a bus up the mountain.

95
00:03:41,002 --> 00:03:43,362
The view is best around sunset.

96
00:03:43,362 --> 00:03:46,529
Cable car and observatory times change with

97
00:03:46,529 --> 00:03:47,399
the season

98
00:03:47,399 --> 00:03:49,748
so check them that morning.

99
00:03:50,178 --> 00:03:52,478
Day three is yours.

100
00:03:52,478 --> 00:03:55,318
Each of these options fills about half a day

101
00:03:55,318 --> 00:03:56,298
so pick two.

102
00:03:56,628 --> 00:03:59,408
Want more history?

103
00:03:59,408 --> 00:04:02,988
Visit Changdeokgung Palace and its Secret Garden.

104
00:04:02,988 --> 00:04:04,988
The garden can only be seen on a guided

105
00:04:04,988 --> 00:04:06,848
tour with its own ticket

106
00:04:06,848 --> 00:04:08,608
and places are limited

107
00:04:08,608 --> 00:04:09,668
so book ahead.

108
00:04:10,134 --> 00:04:13,574
Into design and shopping?

109
00:04:13,574 --> 00:04:15,414
Go to Dongdaemun Design Plaza

110
00:04:15,414 --> 00:04:18,434
and the fashion malls around Dongdaemun that

111
00:04:18,434 --> 00:04:19,654
stay open late.

112
00:04:19,992 --> 00:04:22,472
Want to slow down like a local?

113
00:04:22,472 --> 00:04:24,612
Spend the afternoon in a Han River park

114
00:04:24,612 --> 00:04:25,992
like Yeouido.

115
00:04:25,992 --> 00:04:27,252
People picnic

116
00:04:27,252 --> 00:04:30,212
cycle and order fried chicken to the riverbank.

117
00:04:30,212 --> 00:04:31,272
Renting a bike is easy

118
00:04:31,272 --> 00:04:33,412
and there's always a convenience store nearby.

119
00:04:33,858 --> 00:04:36,738
Or relax properly at a jjimjilbang

120
00:04:36,738 --> 00:04:38,578
a Korean bathhouse.

121
00:04:38,578 --> 00:04:40,258
It's one of the most local things you can

122
00:04:40,258 --> 00:04:41,518
do in Seoul.

123
00:04:41,518 --> 00:04:44,118
Just read up on the etiquette before you go.

124
00:04:44,460 --> 00:04:48,320
Almost everything in this plan is on the subway.

125
00:04:48,320 --> 00:04:50,120
Tap your card in and out at the gates

126
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:52,100
and use the same card on buses.

127
00:04:52,830 --> 00:04:56,159
Taxis are easy to find and fair for short trips.

128
00:04:56,159 --> 00:04:57,683
With the Kakao T app

129
00:04:57,683 --> 00:05:01,030
you can book one without speaking any Korean.

130
00:05:01,584 --> 00:05:02,502
Before you go

131
00:05:02,502 --> 00:05:05,307
here are four small mistakes that catch a lot

132
00:05:05,307 --> 00:05:06,984
of first-time visitors.

133
00:05:08,082 --> 00:05:08,441
One.

134
00:05:08,441 --> 00:05:09,999
Palaces on a weekend.

135
00:05:09,999 --> 00:05:13,951
Most sights are busiest on weekends and public holidays

136
00:05:13,951 --> 00:05:17,126
so do the palaces on a weekday if you can.

137
00:05:17,126 --> 00:05:17,485
Two.

138
00:05:17,485 --> 00:05:19,222
Lunch after two o'clock.

139
00:05:19,222 --> 00:05:22,216
Many restaurants close for a break in the

140
00:05:22,216 --> 00:05:23,953
middle of the afternoon

141
00:05:23,953 --> 00:05:25,391
so eat lunch early.

142
00:05:25,391 --> 00:05:25,870
Three.

143
00:05:25,870 --> 00:05:27,547
No cash at the market.

144
00:05:27,547 --> 00:05:29,583
Cards work almost everywhere

145
00:05:29,583 --> 00:05:32,638
but carry a little cash for market stalls.

146
00:05:32,638 --> 00:05:33,356
And four.

147
00:05:33,356 --> 00:05:35,273
Trusting old opening hours.

148
00:05:35,273 --> 00:05:37,429
Hours and closing days change

149
00:05:37,429 --> 00:05:40,184
so check each place on a map app the

150
00:05:40,184 --> 00:05:41,622
morning you go.

151
00:05:42,036 --> 00:05:45,296
So that's three days in Seoul.

152
00:05:45,296 --> 00:05:47,256
Day one, palaces

153
00:05:47,256 --> 00:05:49,356
hanok lanes and the stream.

154
00:05:49,356 --> 00:05:50,296
Day two

155
00:05:50,296 --> 00:05:51,996
a market breakfast

156
00:05:51,996 --> 00:05:54,776
Myeongdong and the sunset from Namsan.

157
00:05:54,776 --> 00:05:55,956
Day three

158
00:05:55,956 --> 00:05:57,396
whatever you love most.

159
00:05:57,750 --> 00:05:59,210
The full plan

160
00:05:59,210 --> 00:06:01,310
with links for every stop

161
00:06:01,310 --> 00:06:03,310
is on Korea Plainly.

162
00:06:03,310 --> 00:06:05,730
The link is in the description.

163
00:06:05,730 --> 00:06:07,850
Have a wonderful trip to Seoul.

